WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
<v DANA>[curious] If I'm wearing thick gloves, do
I even need a sharps container?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.243
<v RAY>Well, it's a fair question, so let's make
it a real choice. Suppose a plant wants

00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:14.233
<v RAY>to protect its people, but it can only do
one thing. It can hand out heavier

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:17.760
<v RAY>gloves, or it can put sharps containers
on every line.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.680
<v DANA>I think I'd pick the gloves. They're
right there on your hands.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.542
<v RAY>That makes sense, and heavy-duty gloves
do help. They protect you against cuts

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:27.440
<v RAY>and punctures.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.840
<v DANA>[playful] I can hear a "but" coming.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.569
<v RAY>[matter-of-fact] The catch is that a
needle can get through EVEN a thick

00:00:33.569 --> 00:00:37.402
<v RAY>glove. Imagine a needle tip pressed
against a heavy work glove, and it can

00:00:37.402 --> 00:00:38.400
<v RAY>still push through.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.495
<v DANA>[surprised] Huh. I kind of assumed a
thick glove would stop just about

00:00:42.495 --> 00:00:43.040
<v DANA>anything.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.400
<v DANA>So what does the container do that the
glove can't?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.977
<v RAY>A safety-engineered sharps container is
what's called an engineering control.

00:00:50.977 --> 00:00:55.554
<v RAY>That means it works on the sharp itself,
because once the sharp drops in, the

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:57.120
<v RAY>container holds it inside.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.960
<v DANA>So the gloves are on me, and the
container is on the SHARP.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.800
<v RAY>That's really the difference.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.600
<v DANA>So is the glove enough on its own?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.640
<v RAY>No. The gloves still help, but on their
own they give you less protection.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.040
<v DANA>Okay. That changes my answer.

